                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
                from points of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                to the
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/completely+prime+filter"} completely prime filters
                of its open-set lattice is a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijection
            %li
              %p
                (Assuming classical logic) every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/irreducible+closed+set"} irreducible closed set
                (non-empty closed set that is not the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/union"} union
                of any two proper closed subsets) is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+closure"} closure
                of a unique point.
          %p
            In each case, half of the definition is that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
