                  of a point.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#separation Separation
          %ul
            %li
              Sobriety is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separation+property"} separation property
              that is stronger than
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/T0"} T0
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/T1"} T1
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+logic"} classical logic
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+space"} Hausdorff space
              is sober (see at
              = succeed ")," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+implies+sober"} Hausdorff implies sober
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructively
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Hausdorff
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ⇒
                  %mi sober
                  %mo ⇒
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Hausdorff = T_2 \Rightarrow sober \Rightarrow T_0
          %h3#AsLocalesWithEnoughPoints As locales with enough points
          %p
            What makes the concept of sober topological spaces special is that for them the concept of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functions"} continuous functions
            may be expressed entirely in terms of the relations between their
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subsets"} open subsets
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FrameMorphismsBetweenOpensOfSoberSpaces"}
            below), we first introduce the following terminology:
          #HomomorphismOfFramesOfOpens.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi τ
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\tau_X)
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi τ
                      %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Y,\tau_Y)
              be
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi τ
                      %mi X
                    %mo ⟵
                    %msub
                      %mi τ
                      %mi Y
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\tau_X \longleftarrow \tau_Y \;\colon\; \phi
            %p
              between their
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/frame+of+opens"} sets of open subsets
              is called a
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/frame"} frame
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
              if it preserves
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  arbitrary
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unions"} unions
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+number"} finite
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersections"} intersections
            %p
              In other words,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
              is a frame homomorphism if
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  for every
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi I
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
                  and every
                  = succeed "-indexed" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi I
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi τ
                          %mi Y
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi I
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \in \tau_Y\}_{i \in I}
                  of elements of
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi τ
                            %mi Y
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau_Y
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mrow
                          %mo (
                          %munder
                            %mo ∪
                            %mrow
                              %mi i
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi I
                          %msub
                            %mi U
                            %mi i
                          %mo )
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo =
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %munder
                          %mo ∪
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi I
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi τ
                          %mi X
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ,
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\phi\left(\underset{i \in I}{\cup} U_i\right) \;=\; \underset{i \in I}{\cup} \phi(U_i)\;\;\;\;\in \tau_X
                        \\,,
              %li
                %p
                  for every
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+set"} finite set
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi J
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
                  and every
                  = succeed "-indexed" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi J
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi j
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi τ
                          %mi Y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_j \in \tau_Y\}
                  of elements in
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi τ
                            %mi Y
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau_Y
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mrow
                          %mo (
                          %munder
                            %mo ∩
                            %mrow
                              %mi j
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi J
                          %msub
                            %mi U
                            %mi j
                          %mo )
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo =
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %munder
                          %mo ∩
                          %mrow
                            %mi j
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi J
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi τ
                          %mi X
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\phi\left(\underset{j \in J}{\cap} U_j\right)
                        \\;=\;
                        \\underset{j \in J}{\cap} \phi(U_j)
                        \\;\;\;\;\in \tau_X
                        \\,.
          #PreservationOfInclusionsByFrameHomomorphism.num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/frame"} frame
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
              as in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HomomorphismOfFramesOfOpens"}
              necessarily also preserves inclusions in that
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  for every inclusion
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ⊂
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_1 \subset U_2
                  with
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mn 2
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi τ
                          %mi Y
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi P
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_1, U_2 \in \tau_Y \subset P(Y)
                  then
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi τ
                          %mi X
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\phi(U_1) \subset \phi(U_2) \;\;\;\;\;\;\; \in \tau_X
                        \\,.
            %p This is because inclusions are witnessed by unions
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ∪
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mn 2
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mn 2
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (U_1 \subset U_2)
                    \\;\Leftrightarrow\;
                    \\left( U_1 \cup U_2 = U_2 \right)
            %p and by finite intersections:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ∩
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mn 2
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mn 1
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
